text:
The Week Ahead In Technology for November 16, 2026. $NVDA reports without Jensen Huang, and the numbers aren't my worry. It's a stock shock, not a business shock. Will there even be a guide?
Monday I'm on @CNBC Squawk on the Street: NVIDIA and the Anthropic IPO.

$NVDA: supplier commitments more than doubled to $279B, driven mostly by memory. Jensen's calls. Who makes the next one?

@AnthropicAI: IPO expected to price near $1T. Only circular if nobody pays. Somebody is.

@Microsoft Ignite: will we get more insights on how many customers pay for agents by usage, not seats?

Everpure $P: bought components to secure supply; free cash flow went negative. Does it come back?

@Lenovo: record 9.1% infrastructure margin. Does it hold as AI servers ship?

Ian Buck, my top internal pick for NVIDIA CEO, gives its SC26 special address. Who's your pick?

